{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396315-funeral-style-a-martial-art-for-the-dead-and-mourning","id":1396315,"title":"Funeral Style, a Martial Art for the Dead and Mourning","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-13T22:20:18-07:00","id":1396315,"title":"Funeral Style, a Martial Art for the Dead and Mourning","content":"I'm playing a Way of the Long Death monk in D&amp;D 5e when I'm not playing Exalted, and wanted to try my hand at making a Martial Art based off of the subclass. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Funeral Style</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This somber Martial Art is an earthly offshoot of the Violet Bier of Sorrows Style practiced by the Sidereal Exalted. Funeral Style is practiced heavily in Sijan, and has slowly spread as the Sijanese perform esoteric last rites across Creation. The Funeral Style uses nerve strikes, kicks, and swirling footwork to leave enemies in repose. Funeral Stylists that master the Charms hold special powers over ghosts, and easily dispatch zombies and other undead. For that reason, it has proven very popular among the Liminal Exalted, and has even begun to be performed among Death\u2019s Lawgivers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Form Weapons: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This style is most often performed unarmed, though staffs are also a viable weapon.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Armor: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This style can be practiced in Light armor or unarmored.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Complementary abilities: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medicine allows a user to find the nerve clusters on a target, while Occult provides a measure of control over ghosts</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Restful Fist</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3m </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Martial Arts 2, Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aggravated, Dual</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Striking at the spine, the Funeralist separates spirit from body. This attack supplements an attack against a target. On a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attack, this attack deals an extra (Essence/2, minimum 1) post-Soak damage. On a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attack, this attack gains an automatic success on the damage roll, and deals Aggravated damage to ghosts. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Phantasmal Flicker Stance</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2m, 1wp </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Martial Arts 2 Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One tick</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mastery, Dual</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Restful Fist</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dwelling in death, the Funeralist becomes like the ghosts of the forgotten; faded and ungrabbable. Add (Martial Arts/2, rounded down) to Evasion for the duration. Also, increase the difficulty of the grapple Gambit against the Funeralist by (Essence or 3, whichever is lower)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mastery: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The duration is increased to Round, and this Charm\u2019s effects rounds up</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entombing Sweep</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5m, 1i </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Martial Arts 3, Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Decisive-only, Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Phantasmal Flicker Stance</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sweeping for the legs, the Funeralist knocks the target to the ground, like a body lowered into a grave. This Charm creates a Gambit with Difficulty 3. Upon a success, the target is knocked prone. The target cannot attempt to Rise from Prone on their next turn, unless they pay a 1wp surcharge.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Funeral Form</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10m, 1wp </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Martial Arts 3, Ess 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Form, Dual</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entombing Sweep</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Standing with feet at hip\u2019s distance apart, the Funeralist presses their hands together into prayer mudra. Though they seem calm and nonthreatening, they are perfectly posed to strike down anything that approaches. While in Funeral Form, the Martial Artist gains bonus die on attacks against a target equal to (Essence or target\u2019s Wound Penalty, whichever is higher). Additionally, attacks against ghosts that kill the target permanently destroys the spirit. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Activation Rules: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whenever a living creature within Short range of the Martial Artist takes Lethal damage in their Incapaciatated Health Box, this form can be entered reflexively. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Seven Koans of Mourning</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">7m, 1wp </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Martial Arts 3, Ess 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dual, Terrestrial</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Funeral Form</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reciting the Grieving Koans of the Bereaved, the Funarlist forces the souls of the dead to accept their fate, and the souls of the living to dread the end. After landing a successful </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">or </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attack against a target, the Martial Artist rolls (Charisma + Martial Arts) against the Resolve of all hostile targets in Medium range. Living target\u2019s whose Resolve is beaten suffer (Essence) penalty to attack the Martial Artist or her allies for the scene. Undead and ghostly targets suffer the same effect, as well as suffering (Essence) Aggravated damage.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Terrestrial: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The effect extends to Short range.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Grim Kicks of the Six Legged Horse</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10m </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Martial Arts 4, Ess 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Deceive-only, Perilous, Aggravated</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Seven Koans of Mourning</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With a flurry of practiced movements, the Martial Artist batters away life and leaves the body ready for interment. This Charm creates multiple </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attacks against a single target. The amount of attacks is equal to (Martial Arts/2, rounded up). Split the Initiative evenly among all attacks, minimum 3 per attack. Add the Target\u2019s Wound Penalty to the damage of each successful attack. If the attack roll of any of the attacks has three 6s, then add an extra attack. If the user does not have enough Initiative to split for this next attack, it has base damage 3. This Charm deals Aggravated damage against ghosts and other undead beings.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Body-as-Mausoleum Stance</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1wp </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Martial Arts 4, Ess 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Terrestrial</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Grim Kicks of the Six Legged Horse</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Funeralist becomes the house and home of the interred. As such, her flesh is the flesh of the dead, and more resilient to harm. Activate after dealing </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">damage to a target that reduces them to their Incapacitated health box. Gain (target\u2019s Essence +1) -1 health boxes for the scene. Any damage dealt to the Martial Artist happens to these boxes first and heals first. After the scene ends, the damage in the temporary health boxes transfers to the health track, but never enough to put Lethal or Aggravated Damage in the Incapactiated health box.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Terrestrial: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The bonus health is equal to (target\u2019s Essence/2, rounded down, minimum 1)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Saturn\u2019s Gentle Touch (Winter\u2019s Final Caress)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1m, 3a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Martial Arts 5, Ess 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mastery, Terrestrial, Decisive-only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Body-as-Mausoleum Stance</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Maiden of Endings gives a quiet sob as she closes the shears on another thread. The Charm creates a touch Gambit at Difficulty 6. Upon a success, deal (Martial Arts+Essence)L health levels of damage with (Essence)L dice of damage. Any target killed by this technique cannot become a ghost as they are flung into their next life by the force of the attack.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mastery: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If this Charm kills a non-trivial target, the Funeralist may use Entombing Sweep against another target in Short range reflexively and for free. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Terrestrial: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Charm can only be used after dealing Lethal damage to the Incapacitated health box of a non-trivial target this scene.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13696-knurlurzhad","name":"Knurlurzhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}